    ->filter(fn ($idea) => $idea->isUseful())
    ->first();

share($lesson);</code></pre><p>Measure the result before moving on. The goal is to leave the next person, including your future self, with code that explains what it does.</p><h2 id="takeaway">What I’m taking forward</h2><p>Progress is often a collection of small improvements. Keep the useful ones, question the complicated ones, and share the reasoning behind your choices.</p><p>What has worked for you? I’d love to hear how you approach this in your own projects.</p><div class="article-demo-note">Sample article for the UI preview. Full author content will come from the publishing backend.</div></div>
